  "description": "Hand-written ASN.1 Basic Encoding Rules (BER) codec: TLV primitives and SEQUENCE/CHOICE/SET helpers shared by the Presentation, ACSE, and MMS layers (Session framing uses its own SPDU/parameter encoding, not ASN.1 BER, so it is deliberately not a consumer of this module). This is the highest-risk, highest-value module in the stack -- correctness here is validated continuously against Wireshark captures, golden binary vectors, and fuzzing (starting in Phase 2B, per the roadmap).",
